Add support ticket system backend API (prompt 1 of 3)

New files:
- backend/support_api.py: AI-first support system with knowledge base
- supabase/migrations/018_support_system.sql: tables for articles,
  conversations, and messages

User endpoints (/v1/support/):
- POST /chat: AI-powered support chat with auto-escalation
- POST /escalate: explicit escalation to human
- GET /conversations: list user's conversations
- GET /conversations/{id}: get conversation with messages
- GET /articles: browse published help articles
- GET /articles/{id}: read full article

Admin endpoints (/v1/admin/support/):
- GET /tickets: list all tickets with filters
- GET /tickets/{id}: full ticket with internal notes
- POST /tickets/{id}/reply: admin reply (or internal note)
- PUT /tickets/{id}/status: update status/priority
- POST /tickets/{id}/ai-draft: AI-drafted response suggestion
- GET /stats: dashboard statistics
- CRUD on /articles: knowledge base management

AI agent references knowledge base articles, parses category and
confidence metadata, and auto-escalates when it can't help or the
user requests a human.
